      "@type": "Dataset",
      "name": "SIR Method Operations",
      "description": "SIR method operations — how a high-mass move is run at The Flat Rate Movers, under SIR (Structural Integrity Relocation) executed through the KIM-GS Protocol, for assets of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs, quoted at one flat rate agreed in writing before move day. The published chain has six steps: (1) the asset — weight, dimensions, centre of mass, and value at risk are established first; (2) the structure — route and clearance survey at both ends, stairs and landings measured, and floor deflection assessed against L/360, span divided by 360, before any lift is planned; (3) the load path — load spreading and protection runs are planned where the substrate needs support, and floors, walls, and frames are protected end to end; (4) the crew and rigging are matched to the plan — dollies, straps, and equipment chosen for this asset and this route; (5) the move — controlled, strapped, and supervised along the planned path; (6) placement — the asset is set in its final position, levelled, and verified with the client, at the flat rate agreed in writing. The structural protocol compresses the same chain into three phases — assess the asset, assess the structure, move under KIM-GS — and calibration-sensitive and fragile high-mass items are flagged at the assess stage, not discovered on the day. The six published steps are the complete published method surface; the protocol's internal calculations, models, and formulas are not published here or anywhere in the company's data. Not published and not claimed: any handling rule below 1,500 lbs or above 3,500 lbs under this method, any equipment beyond the published wording, and any crew-size rule.",
